5. Conclusion: The Duty to Restore Reality
The research suggests that the only moral path forward is the restoration of the truth. Because the "victim" in this scenario is being denied the right to their own perception and their own body, the witness holds the "key" to their liberation. Telling the truth is not an act of betrayal against the friend; it is an act of justice for the partner whose free will has been stolen.
